description: Commit structure and conventional commits
alwaysApply: false
---

## Principles

- One logical change per commit; split infra, docs, config, and features when practical.
- Conventional Commits: `feat|fix|docs|chore|ci|test|refactor|build(scope): description`
- Order: foundation (CI/scripts) → implementation → docs.
- Stage explicit paths; avoid `git add .`.
- Run `npm run format:check` before each commit.

## Split when

- CI/workflows vs feature code vs docs (small doc fixes tied to the feature may stay together).
- Different features → separate commits.

## Gotchas

- Tightly coupled changes may be one commit.
- Do not commit with format failures.
